      en: ["Highest peak on Boa Vista Island at 387 meters.", "Composed of volcanic phonolitic rock formations.", "Habitat for rare endemic plants like Lavandula rotundifolia.", "Located in the southeastern quadrant of Boa Vista.", "Historically used as a lookout for maritime threats.", "Part of the protected Monte Estância Natural Monument."],
